.TH TWEETA-DESKTOP 1 "19 February 2026" "tweeta-desktop" "Tweeta User Manual"
.SH NAME
tweeta-desktop \- GTK3 desktop client for Tweeta/Tweetapus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tweeta-desktop
.RI [ GTK_OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tweeta-desktop
is a GTK3 desktop client for the Tweeta/Tweetapus social platform.
.SH FEATURES
.PP
Current application features include:
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
Public and following timelines with infinite scroll.
.IP \(bu 2
User authentication (login/logout) with persisted session restore.
.IP \(bu 2
Composing posts with optional media uploads.
.IP \(bu 2
Tweet interactions: reply, like, retweet/quote, bookmark, and emoji reactions.
.IP \(bu 2
Search for users and posts.
.IP \(bu 2
Profile views with tweets/replies/followers/following and follow/unfollow actions.
.IP \(bu 2
Notifications inbox with "mark all as read".
.IP \(bu 2
Direct messaging, including an encrypted messaging workspace (GPG key setup/import and contact management).
.IP \(bu 2
Communities browsing, join/leave, and community timelines.
.IP \(bu 2
Poll rendering and voting in timelines.
.IP \(bu 2
Admin views for stats, users, posts, and post notes/moderation actions.
.IP \(bu 2
Settings for theme, compact mode, notification toggles, and cache cleanup.
.SH OPTIONS
.B tweeta-desktop
does not define custom command-line options.
It accepts standard GTK+ 3 command-line options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TWEETA_API_BASE_URL
Overrides the default API base URL used for API requests.
.TP
.B TWEETA_BASE_DOMAIN
Overrides the default site base domain used for absolute web/media URLs.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory used by GLib for per-user configuration.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory used by GLib for per-user cache data.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tweeta-desktop/session.json
Stores session token, username, and admin flag after a successful login.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/tweeta-desktop/
Cache directory used by cache management in the Settings view.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/pixmaps/tweeta-desktop.png
Installed application icon (location varies by install prefix).
.SH NOTES
Primary runtime support is Linux.
.PP
Encrypted messaging features depend on a working GPGME/GnuPG environment.
